course: dictionary
lesson: 9295
title: Speaking, one word with many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Speaking» is the -ing form of «speak», which means to say words or to talk. Because one word can have several meanings, look at the words around it to find the right one.
explain: «Public speaking» is the skill of talking to a group, so the sentence is about talking well in front of people. «An English-speaking country» uses -speaking to mean the country uses English.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Generally speaking, the day was fine» means usually the day was fine, and that still makes sense. «Speaking!» on the phone means «This is me», so the clue is that someone is answering a call.
fact: «Speaking» is the -ing form of the verb «speak».
fact: «Speak» means to say words or to talk.
fact: «Public speaking» is the skill of talking to a group.
fact: «English-speaking» means using English, as in «English-speaking countries».
fact: «Generally speaking» means usually, and «strictly speaking» means if we are exact.
exercise: In class, «speaking and listening» is a key skill. What does speaking mean here? | *Talking clearly and taking turns | Painting a picture | Sleeping quietly at your desk
exercise: Ana picks up the phone and says, «Speaking!» What does she mean? | Goodbye, I am leaving | Speak to me later | *This is me | Please wait a moment
exercise: «Generally speaking, the shop is open on Sundays.» What does «generally speaking» mean? | Loudly and clearly | Never | *Usually | Strictly, to the exact letter
test: Ben and Sam stopped talking after a fight. Ben says, «We're not speaking.» What does that mean? | They are talking very quietly | They are speaking French | *They have fallen out | They are on the phone
test: Which of these is an English-speaking country? | Germany | *Australia | Spain | Japan
exam: «Strictly speaking, the letter Z is "zed" in Britain.» What does «strictly speaking» mean here? | Usually, on most days | Loudly and clearly | Quietly, in a whisper | *If we are exact
